Wrong (A): Outright gifts use the GSTT exemption but expose future appreciation to GSTT at the next generational transfer, making them less tax-efficient than a dynasty trust.
Wrong (B): Re-gifting through children triggers two layers of gift tax and does not avoid GSTT because the ultimate transfer to grandchildren is still a generation-skipping transfer.
