-- Q4020: Wealth Transfer and Gifting Strategies [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sec. 2611, generation-skipping transfers include direct skips (Sec. 2612(c)), taxable distributions (Sec. 2612(b)), and taxable terminations (Sec. 2612(a)). A gift from parent to child is not a GST because the child is only one generation below the transferor under Sec. 2651 and is not a skip person.
Wrong (A): A taxable distribution from a trust to a grandchild is a GST under Sec. 2612(b) because the grandchild is a skip person two generations below the transferor.
Wrong (B): A taxable termination under Sec. 2612(a) occurs when the last non-skip beneficiary''s interest ends and is a recognized type of GST.
Wrong (C): A direct skip gift to a grandchild is a GST under Sec. 2612(c) because it is a transfer directly to a skip person.$EXPL$
